                <pb facs="0800" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 211.52L89/2.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister of
                    Spain.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your request made to-day at
                    the Department for the arrest at New York of Tómas Loscesta and Lazareto Calvo,
                    charged in Spain with fraud, I have the honor to inclose copy of a telegram
                    which has been sent to the Attorney General asking that the United States
                    attorney at New York be instructed by telegraph to take the matter up with the
                    Spanish consul general and to assist him in securing the arrest of the accused
                    parties, in pursuance of article 13 of the extradition treaty between Spain and
                    the United States. I also transmit herewith copy of the form of preliminary
                    mandate.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
